John Lerchey writes:
>I _do_ kind of like the concept of two weapons though.  Perhaps the
>thief class should fight Florentine with a rapier and a dagger, striking
>twice every time he attacks?

From what I remember of AD&D (and I haven't played in over 5 years), it
DOES allow a character to a weapon in either hand. It required a minimum
15 DEX and each attack was subject to modifiers "to hit" which became less
severe with increasing DEX - I think DEX 19 gave you -1/+0. Perhaps a
secondary WIELD command (#WieldLeft or some such?) with a limit on what
can be used in the off hand (suggest dagger at least, maybe up to a
shortsword at most).

Shame Nethack doesn't have the old Runequest (still my favourite game 
system) idea of fumbles:
You attack the frost giant.  You miss wildly! -More-
The dagger in your left hand slashes your flailing right arm! -More-
The tendons are severed -More-
Your useless right arm drops your sword -More-
The frost giant hits! The frost giant hits! -More-
You die...
Then again, maybe it's not such a shame after all! ;-?

